      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1903-03-27_WidnesExaminer_art0022" n="art0022">
        <head>CHAPTER VIII.</head>
        <p>CHAPTER VIII.</p>
        <p>A STRANGE CONVERSATION.</p>
        <p>Mr. Harmaford sat there covering his face with his hand as 'though to Shut out the sight of the girl. Dora stood quietly where she was, and looked at him curiously. She had seen him often at church, and in the street, but never so close. He was handsome in a severe way, with his iron- grey hair cut short in a military fashion, and his moustache pointed smartly. His figure Was good, and eclat as it was h 9. `had already dressed for dinner. Everything about nun was -neat and clean, and he looked a singularly distinguished and handsome old gentleman. Dora, timid by nature, would have bien afraid of him., but she was too anxious about Will to think of fear. After a time he stood up, and reached for a chair. "Please sit down, Miss Tremewan," he said, formally. "I should not have kept you standing." He paused, and looked at her strangely. "But old ullmories, you know." "I was never so handsome as my mother," said Dora, taking the seat: Harmaford started and laughed. "Ah ! I sec you know," said lie; "your mother told you, of caurse,—that is, she torn you her ver.iion." Dora- felt uncomfortable under his gaze, and changed the conversation. "I think it is best to tell you why I came, Mr. Hannaford. It was not to talk about my mother's past." "Or about mine," he said, quickly. "Well, I never supposed it (was. But if you know what you say you know, Miss Tremewan,—that I was one en- gaged to your mother, and was her slave until your father stale her from me—l ,wonder that you care to enter my house." "I never knew you had been engaged to my mother !" said Dora, amazed. "No," replied Hannaford, and shrugged his lean shoulders," of course not. I knew she would give her version of the business. But this is not to the point. lam getting old, I think, when I babble so much." His eyes wandered round the roma Tagely. "Besides, I have been upsetir he said, in a troulalacl way: "gamed:tin:: has haVne...l "</p>
      </div>
