        <head>LORD AND LADY CARDIGAN</head>
        <p>LORD AND LADY CARDIGAN</p>
        <p>Stark's, North Audlev Street. The ceremony W,as performed by 'Canon Fleming and the R. H. Hadden, Chaplain-in-Ordinary to :,11a King; and the bride was attended by -;•A'ree pages and six little bridesmaids. Lord .-udlow, who is married to Lady Howard de \N I b: den this week, attended the bridegroom as 4st tuan ; and amongst the well-known guests 1-.,'re the Duke and Duchess of Newcastle, the '-'nke and 'Duchess of Montrose, the Marquis and Marchioness of Ely, Lord and Lady IVolsely, and many others. Lord Cardigan served out in South Africa during the recent war in the i ith Hussars.</p>
