      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1903-03-27_WidnesExaminer_art0036" n="art0036">
        <head>NEW MEMBER FOR FERMANAGH.</head>
        <p>THE NEW MEMBER FOR FERMANAGH.</p>
        <p>Mr. Mitchell's success in North Ferman- agh is really another rebuff for the Govern- ment. Captain Craig was the man of their party, and his success was officially desired. Mr. Mitchell, on the other hand, was the candidate of the Land Purchase Association, and he stood with the active sup- port of Mr. 'I% W. Russell. Mr: Edward Mi t - chell, the new member, is a native of County Fermanagh, and was educated at F iv emilet own. At Derryvellum, where he re- sides, he has ex, tensive grazing- and he is one of the most prom- inent horse- breeders in Ire- land. He is MR. E. MITCHELL, M.P. the owner of a number of thoroughbred sires, of. which Royal Mask has been champion of Ireland two years. A mem- ber of the Farmanagh grand jury, hc was co-opted on the Council when the new Irish Local Government Act came into operation. Last year he stood as candidate for the County Council, but was defeated by Sir Douglas Brooke. There was a great deal of excitement in the streets when the result of the poll was declared. Mr. Wood, M.P., speaking from" the Court-house, said the result of the election was the worse blow landlordism had sustained for many days. He thanked the Nationalist electors sincerely. Mr. Russell, M.P.,. addrested a large crov,-(1 from the Town Hall.</p>
